## `test-isa-call`

Prefer `@test value isa Type` to `@test isa(value, Type)`. The rule requires a visible `Test` import and offers a safe fix that preserves the operands and their precedence.

Using `isa` as an operator in a test:

```julia
using Test
@test isa(result, AbstractVector)
```

```text
warning: test-isa-call
 --> example.jl:2:7
  |
2 | @test isa(result, AbstractVector)
  |       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ write `result isa AbstractVector` instead of calling `isa`
  = help: Rewrite as an `isa` comparison (safe fix)
```

After applying the fix:

```julia
using Test
@test result isa AbstractVector
```
